# Slice 297 probe (REPEATED-DECL-TYPED-RECEPTION, the single-field form; the book provenance :428, :483): `char: z` after
# `int: z 5`, the char -> int receiver defined -- the known place is compatible and nothing is written: z stays 5 (the receiver
# adds 100, 105 would be a write through it).  Exit: z's value.
fn: lm_stg_convert_char_int (char: c) int
    return: (cast: (int) c) + 100
end: lm_stg_convert_char_int
fn: run () int
    int: z 5
    char: z
    return: z
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
